r for time","text":"The class starts at eleven o'clock."}]},{"body":"- Write the number as a digit when you can.\n- The digit matches the spoken word.\n- Practice matching the word to the digit.","heading":"Writing the digits","examples":[{"note":"Shows the digit for twenty","text":"20 = twenty"},{"note":"Shows the digit for thirteen","text":"13 = thirteen"}]}],"keyPoints":["eleven to twenty are single words, not \"ten‑one\" etc.","the \"th\" sound in thirteen is soft, like in think","eleven is stressed on the second syllable (e-LEV-en); thirteen to nineteen are stressed on -teen when said alone (thir-TEEN), and the stress may move to the first syllable before a noun","place the number word before the noun","the digit 13 matches the word thirteen"],"commonMistakes":[{"why":"Arabic speakers often translate the pattern of 10 + 1","right":"eleven","wrong":"one ten"},{"why":"The word twenty stands alone, not twenty‑one","right":"twenty","wrong":"twenty‑one for 20"},{"why":"The ordinal form (fifteenth) is different from the cardinal (fifteen)","right":"fifteen","wrong":"saying \"fifteenth\" for 15"}]}$aimfix$::jsonb,
